{
  "description": "#5140 Phase 4a — `apply_page_source` saves a page edited as its source buffer: the text `get_page_buffer` gives, with the id each of its lines carries in `lineIds` (#5160 A), is diffed against the page's own render by id, and the difference is written as edits, moves, creates and deletes. Covers only what the tauri mock models, so every seeded block is plain single-line text (no task markers, list styles, properties or names, and no `[[`, `#`, `->` or `::`), which both stacks' `get_page_source` render byte for byte as `- content ^ID`, a further line indented under its bullet; the ids are the seed labels' expanded ids. Each successful step's `baseSource` is the page's source after the step before it, so every step also passes the stale check; the create runs last because its block's id is minted per stack. One kind of change per step, so the op log's order does not depend on the order the command writes kinds in, and the delete is kept out of a reordered sibling group. Seed: S1 (Home) > S2 (alpha), S3 (bravo), S4 (charlie), S5 (delta) > S6 (echo). Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
